{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c503","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075af-a7c5-7382-ae46-5efb02855e33"},"sequence":220,"recorded_at":1780531400000435,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"26b812e8-1ff5-438a-879f-a23352be1f58"},"task_id":"26b812e8-1ff5-438a-879f-a23352be1f58","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"26b812e8-1ff5-438a-879f-a23352be1f58","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-11-1\",\n  \"command\": \"echo \\\"BOARD=$TASK_BOARD_DIR\\\"; ls \\\"$TASK_BOARD_DIR\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 20; echo ===; task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-ljkj8r) { full }' 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(list(d.keys())); import json as j; print(j.dumps(d, indent=1)[:9000])\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Locate board dir and dump task JSON\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"BOARD=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board\\nEPIC-260829-dz9yvx_implementation-repository-foundation\\nEPIC-260830-1ewjla_advisory-human-validation\\nEPIC-260830-1uwj54_m1-single-host-durability\\nEPIC-260830-27bix9_m3-daily-driver-tmux\\nEPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation\\nEPIC-260830-391tge_m4-cloning-directory-platform-release-hardening\\nEPIC-260830-3v9jlg_m2-multi-host-preview\\n===\\n['ac', 'assignee', 'blockedBy', 'blocks', 'checklist', 'children', 'created', 'derivedBlockedBy', 'derivedBlocks', 'description', 'estimate', 'id', 'integrationCheckpointed', 'isAdvisoryBlocked', 'isBlocked', 'name', 'notes', 'observability', 'outcomeResources', 'parent', 'preconditionResources', 'review', 'scope', 'status', 'task_class', 'title', 'type', 'updated']\\n{\\n \\\"ac\\\": \\\"Production behavior demonstrates: Implement Directory Node major bootstrap, manifest/probe/scan/query operation framing, host checks, and structured errors. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\\\",\\n \\\"assignee\\\": \\\"[implementer] developer (muse)\\\",\\n \\\"blockedBy\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260830-2z3se0\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"blocks\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260830-3bkz0c\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"checklist\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Implement Directory Node major bootstrap, manifest/probe/scan/query operation framing, host checks, and structured errors\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio \\\\u2014 `n of m AC rows driven` \\\\u2014 and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant \\\\u2014 the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Lint clean\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Tests green\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read \\\\u2014 positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"If review does not accept the work \\\\u2014 verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"children\\\": [],\\n \\\"created\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T22:00:06Z\\\",\\n \\\"derivedBlockedBy\\\": [],\\n \\\"derivedBlocks\\\": [],\\n \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement Directory Node major bootstrap, manifest/probe/scan/query operation framing, host checks, and structured errors. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\\\",\\n \\\"estimate\\\": {\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"estimated\\\",\\n  \\\"scale\\\": {\\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fibonacci\\\",\\n   \\\"number\\\": 8\\n  }\\n },\\n \\\"id\\\": \\\"TASK-260830-ljkj8r\\\",\\n \\\"integrationCheckpointed\\\": false,\\n \\\"isAdvisoryBlocked\\\": false,\\n \\\"isBlocked\\\": false,\\n \\\"name\\\": \\\"implement-directory-node-protocol-host\\\",\\n \\\"notes\\\": \\\"spawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/xhigh pair_source=explicit match=not_recommended snapshot=sha256:08c5d671a0c9e2350b1b8c97c08841f378392d0f4ac8edf05ecf155d29ae97bb rationale=\\\\\\\"implementation class rank 1; second leaf, inheriting leaf 1's enumerated censuses\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=muse; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260906-25c417, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260906-25c417)\\\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (muse) (exit=0)\\\\nspawn run completed: muse (run=RUN-260906-25c417, pid=86389, exit=0)\\\\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=claude/claude-opus-5/xhigh pair_source=explicit match=not_recommended snapshot=sha256:1d432acfa5b6f6101ec00874dad940578fb6cb015296a686a5e0a3b9569d548b rationale=\\\\\\\"review class rank 1; second leaf, whether leaf 1's census discipline transferred\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1-128-gab60e0d; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (run=RUN-260906-ccfe0d, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (run=RUN-260906-ccfe0d)\\\\nREVIEW rev1 (RUN-260906-ccfe0d): CHANGES REQUESTED -> to-dev. repeat-of: none (first round of this leaf); class-of leaf 1 rev3-B5/rev4-B8.\\\\n\\\\nB1 (blocking) Bound edges unwitnessed as a class. 94 one-step bound mutants across manifest/probe/scan/query/protocol: 19 killed, 75 SURVIVED (0 NOT_APPLIED, 0 COMPILE_FAIL). Survivors by file: query 43, manifest 13, probe 12, scan 7. Bounds are correct and reachable - 4 representative out-of-range values are refused today at the production entry - so the gap is the evidence. Leaf 1 carries bound_census_test.go (1650 lines) + bounds_edge_test.go (423 lines) for exactly this class; dirnode has neither. Same mutant shape (checkStringBounds max +1) is KILLED in sessadapter and SURVIVES at every checkStringBounds maximum in dirnode. TestManifestLimitsBounds doc claims each bound refuses past its edge in both directions; 4 of its 14 edges are unprobed and all 4 survive.\\\\n\\\\nB2 (blocking) AC row 5 17-op union not driven. 5 of 17 query operations reach DecodeQuery (schema, sessions, set_title, plan_continue, execute_plan); 12 undriven with no stated bound. Ten production functions at 0.0% coverage, all 10.8.5 union validators. Three narrowing mutants inside them (environments auth_status admits root; jobs states admits pwned; distinct field admits secret) all survive. Whole class funnels into one census arm with 4 witnesses, so the census reads complete while 10 validators have never executed - the leaf-1 wrapper shape in new clothes.\\