{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075af-a7c5-7382-ae46-5efb02855e33"},"sequence":282,"recorded_at":1780531400000559,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"dff3d35e-7c98-45bf-a3b2-fcd567481990"},"task_id":"dff3d35e-7c98-45bf-a3b2-fcd567481990","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"dff3d35e-7c98-45bf-a3b2-fcd567481990","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/ljkj8r/TASK-260830-ljkj8r_round2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework — review response (B1/B2/B3)\n2|\n3|Production code is unchanged from the reviewed candidate: all rework is\n4|tests plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes. Working tree holds the\n5|rework uncommitted per the brief.\n6|\n7|## B1 — bound instrument ported (blocking, now closed)\n8|\n9|- `internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go`: production-derived bound census,\n10|  101 sites (9 helpers + len/length-var guards), 72 driven + 29 exempt\n11|  (mechanism/plumbing with rationale). Census fails closed on unregistered\n12|  sites, orphaned rows, helper aliases, and unscanned files.\n13|- `internal/dirnode/bounds_edge_test.go`: edge drivers for every driven row\n14|  (min-1/min/max/max+1 through the production entry).\n15|- Battery: 185 applied / 142 killed / 43 equivalent-with-bound / 0 survivors,\n16|  zero not-applied, zero compile failures. Denominator derived from\n17|  production (scanner output), not listed.\n18|- Census-only kills scored separately: 2 live census mutants redden only\n19|  `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused` (unregistered site; helper alias), plus the\n20|  three synthetic gate proofs. Behavioural kills (142) all fail a driver\n21|  that exercises the production entry.\n22|\n23|## B2 — seventeen-operation obligation set derived and driven (blocking, now closed)\n24|\n25|- `internal/dirnode/query_operations_test.go`: `TestDecodeQueryAllOperationsAdmit`\n26|  drives 17/17 registry members (was 5/17 reaching DecodeQuery) with kind\n27|  checks; `TestDecodeQueryOperationValidatorsRefuse` drives 40+\n28|  validator-specific defects; projection/sort/pagination/lineage/count\n29|  rules pinned alongside.\n30|- Zero-coverage functions before: validQueryField, checkLineageParameters,\n31|  checkHostsParameters, checkEnvironmentsParameters, checkJobsParameters,\n32|  checkPlansParameters, checkDistinctParameters, checkTagsParameter,\n33|  checkPinParameter, checkEnrichParameters (10 at 0.0%). After: none at 0.0%.\n34|- Review narrowing probes are battery rows V01 (environments/\"root\"),\n35|  V02 (jobs/\"pwned\"), V03 (distinct/\"secret\"): all killed.\n36|\n37|## B3 — arm-slide vectors fixed (blocking, now closed)\n38|\n39|- `unknown_field` rebuilt without the duplicate `fields` member; new\n40|  `TestUnknownFieldVectorReachesTheFieldRegistry` proves the operation\n41|  object passes the strict decoder (single `fields`) before DecodeQuery\n42|  refuses, so the field registry is reached, not the duplicate gate.\n43|- Audit found the same rename-instead-of-delete slide in three more\n44|  vectors (query \"missing caller\", manifest \"missing member\", probe\n45|  response \"missing member\"): each renamed member fired the unknown arm\n46|  while witnessing the missing arm. All three now delete the member, and\n47|  `TestMissingVectorsDriveTheMissingArm` asserts the missing-member message.\n48|- Scan/probe-request missing vectors already delete; unknown vectors add\n49|  exactly one member. Protocol `relabeled major pair` placeholder is\n50|  overridden with a genuine relabeled frame (verified, no change needed).\n51|\n52|## AC coverage — 9 of 9 rows driven through production entries\n53|\n54|| AC row | production call site | named t