{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c583","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075af-a7c5-7382-ae46-5efb02855e33"},"sequence":284,"recorded_at":1780531400000563,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589"},"call_id":"call_01a075b0b26f7a429b5c36a17e7c5c45","text":"Read text file `/tmp/ljkj8r/TASK-260830-ljkj8r_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-ljkj8r — reviewer verdict, CR rev2\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`.**\n4|**repeat-of: rev1-B3 (C1 below) and rev1-B2 (C2 below).** Two consecutive\n5|same-class findings: the next step is a derived gate, not another hand audit.\n6|Evidence: `TASK-260830-ljkj8r_review-mutant-log-rev2.md`.\n7|\n8|Candidate tree `bd3cb8c05f421365e1e20f9e18ad53cb13d33d18` verified\n9|byte-identical before and after all 433 mutant applications.\n10|`repository_delta=present`, 27 paths; production code is byte-identical to\n11|rev1 (`git diff 4d8a599 bd3cb8c` touches only test files and `LOGBOOK.md`).\n12|Delta 23 → 27 = `arm_identity_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`,\n13|`bounds_edge_test.go`, `query_operations_test.go`; four already-present test\n14|files carry the vector surgery, `LOGBOOK.md` the round entry. Fully accounted.\n15|\n16|Suite re-run on my own machine: `go test ./... -count=1` 18 packages ok,\n17|`go vet ./...` exit 0, `gofmt -l internal/` clean,\n18|`go test ./internal/dirnode -cover` 83.3%. All three producer claims reproduce.\n19|\n20|---\n21|\n22|## G-A — the instrument transferred. B1 is CLOSED.\n23|\n24|**The shape space is this package's own, not leaf 1's list.** It enumerates ten\n25|shapes against `dirnode` constructs that do not exist in `sessadapter` —\n26|`checkURI`, `CheckCursorReuse`'s character measure, `Journal.Import`'s ordering\n27|gate, `skip > 1000000`, `index > 63`, `version != 1` — and marks six derived,\n28|four stated, with a live-instance claim per shape. Three synthetic suites prove\n29|the derivation halves (indirection, non-`if` contexts, length variables), 11\n30|canaries fail the census closed if the scanner goes blind, and an empty scan\n31|fails. 101 sites rostered, 72 driven, 29 exempt with rationales.\n32|\n33|**Ratio over the identical production-derived denominator: 68 of 94 killed\n34|(was 19 of 94).** 0 NOT_APPLIED, 0 COMPILE_FAIL, **0 resurrections** — all 19\n35|rev1 kills are still killed. The `checkStringBounds max +1` mutant that\n36|survived on every maximum in rev1 now dies on every one.\n37|\n38|All 26 survivors map 1:1 onto declared `equiv-ok` rows, and I verified each\n39|masking gate in production source rather than accepting the rationale:\n40|`environmentIDPattern` `{0,63}`, `providerIDPattern` `{0,31}`, `checkSemver`'s\n41|5-character floor, the 8/5/4/7/3-member closed tables, the 27-field registry,\n42|and the joint count/index gate at 65 (both tightenings die). No false\n43|equivalence.\n44|\n45|**The wrapper shape is closed here.** `checkURI` is this package's\n46|`requireStringBounds` — a forwarder carrying its own `1..512` literals,\n47|exempted as \"mechanism\". Its ceiling dies in both directions and its floor dies\n48|at `<4`. Leaf 1's 25-of-46 survivor shape does not recur.\n49|\n50|I extended the battery to the 54 sites rev1 never touched (len guards, wrapper\n51|internals, shape-7/8/10 stated bounds): 42 killed. The findings below come from\n52|there and from two further production-derived sweeps.\n53|\n54|---\n55|\n56|## C1 (blocking) — the arm-slide sweep was reported as covering a class it did not cover. **repeat-of rev1-B3.**\n57|\n58|The B3 vector itself is fixed and pinned by construction, and the three\n59|rename→delete missing vectors are pinned by message. Verified: all four arms die\n60|under deletion. But the audit note in `arm_identity_test.go` states the rest of\n61|the class clean —\n62|\n63|> \"every 'unknown member' vector adds exactly one member, so those reach the\n64|> arm they name\"\n65|\n66|— and that is false for three of them. Driven through the production entry,\n67|unmutated:\n68|\n69|| vector | arm it names | arm it actually reaches |\n70||---|---|---|\n71|| `manifest_test.go:62` \"unknown member\" | `unknownMember` (`manifest.go:268`) | `node manifest trailing data after the object` — the replacement `\"limits\":{` → `\"limits\":{},\"extra\":1,` hoists every limits member to the top level and leaves malformed JSON |\n72|| `query_test.go:75` \"unknown member\" | `unknownMember` (`query.go:415`) | `directory query operation is not a closed QueryOperation` — the `\"extensions\":{}}` needle matches `operations[0].parameters` first, never the envelope |\n73|| `probe_test.go:142` \"unknown member\" | `unknownMember` (`probe.go:338`) | `probe response node build is not the closed DirectoryNodeBuild` — the needle matches `node_build` first |\n74|\n75|Independently: a 144-arm reachability sweep (every production `if` whose body\n76|builds a `failX`, derived by AST; 115 killed / 144, 0 unmeasured) finds those\n77|three envelope-level `unknownMember` arms deletable with a green suite, plus:\n78|\n79|- **5 `missingMember` arms deletable** — `probe.go:141`, `protocol.go:428`,\n80|  `protocol.go:559`, `scan.go:78`, `scan.go:193`. These vectors *do* reach the\n81|  right arm today (I confirmed all four report `misses a required member`), but\n82|  their assertions check code + detail member only, and a deleted member also\n83|  refuses downstream. The three vectors round 2 fixed die only because round 2\n84|  added a message assertion; the same assertion was not extended to the rest of\n85|  the class.\n86|- **2 gates with zero negative coverage** — `checkExtensions` on the probe\n87|  response (`probe.go:392`) and on the query envelope (`query.go:467`). The\n88|  gates work (a `\"NOTDNS\"` key gives `probe response extensions are not\n89|  reverse-DNS keyed`), but deleting either keeps the suite green. Their four\n90|  siblings — manifest, probe request, scan request, scan response — are all\n91|  covered, so this is a class closed at four of six.\n92|- **3 empty-frame arms deletable** — `bootstrap.go:144`, `protocol.go:399`,\n93|  `protocol.go:530`. All three are census rows marked *driven*;\n94|  `TestFrameBoundEdges` asserts only `err != nil`, and an empty frame also fails\n95|  the strict decoder, so the named driver cannot fail.\n96|\n97|What to change: derive the vector-reachability gate instead of auditing it by\n98|hand. Every fixture-surgery vector that names an arm should assert that arm's\n99|message, the way `TestMissingVectorsDriveTheMissingArm` does for three — and\n100|the arm roster should fail closed when an arm has no vector that fires it.\n101|\n102|---\n103|\n104|## C2 (blocking) — B2 closed the admissions, not the obligations. **repeat-of rev1-B2.**\n105|\n106|The 17-operation *admission* set is genuinely derived: the union is built from\n107|the production `readOperations` + `mutationOperations` tables and fails closed\n108|when an operation has no builder. 17 of 17 admit. The three named narrowing\n109|probes — `\"root\"`, `\"pwned\"`, `\"secret\"` — are rows and die. That half is real.\n110|\n111|The *refusal* set is a 45-row hand table with no production-derived\n112|denominator. Measured against one — every `return false` in `query.go`, one\n113|mutant per site, `return false` → `return true`:\n114|\n115|**58 of 89 obligations driven; 31 removable with a green suite.**\n116|\n117|| validator | obligations | driven | undriven |\n118||---|---:|---:|---:|\n119|| `checkPlanContinueParameters` | 9 | 3 | 6 |\n120|| `checkQuerySort` | 8 | 3 | 5 |\n121|| `checkFilters` | 16 | 13 | 3 |\n122|| `checkQueryParameters` | 5 | 2 | 3 |\n123|| `checkExecutePlanParameters` | 5 | 2 | 3 |\n124|| `checkSubject` | 4 | 1 | 3 |\n125|| `checkUUIDv7DigestSubset` | 5 | 3 | 2 |\n126|| `checkQueryFlags` | 3 | 1 | 2 |\n127|| `checkTagsParameter`, `checkLineageParameters`, `checkDistinctParameters`, `isAnnotationMutation` | 8 | 4 | 4 |\n128|| 11 validators at full coverage | 26 | 26 | 0 |\n129|| **total** | **89** | **58** | **31** |\n130|\n131|`plan_continue` is the sharpest instance: it admits positively and its three\n132|closed vocabularies refuse, but all six member-shape checks\n133|(`source_instance_id` digest, `to_host_id` UUIDv7, `to_installation_id` digest,\n134|and the three `rawString` type reads) can be deleted with a green suite. That\n135|is positive-path-only evidence for one of the seventeen operations.\n136|\n137|And the answer to the question as asked — **yes, one arm still carries N of\n138|them**: all 89 obligations still report through the single\n139|`checkQueryOperation` arm. Coverage moved (10 functions off 0.0%, package\n140|83.3%); the obligation ratio is 65%.\n141|\n142|---\n143|\n144|## C3 (blocking) — the uniqueness half of the sorted-unique class is closed at one of eight sites.\n145|\n146|`>=` → `>` in a pairwise ordering scan keeps the gate present and weakens it to\n147|admit exactly one member of the class it must reject: a duplicate. Production\n148|refuses duplicates today. Seven of eight survive:\n149|\n150|| site | member class | `>=`→`>` |\n151||---|---|---|\n152|| `decode.go:377` `checkSortedUniqueStrings` | every sorted-unique string array | **KILLED** |\n153|| `decode.go:403` `checkSortedUniqueDigests` | every digest array | SURVIVED |\n154|| `decode.go:429` `checkSortedUniqueUUIDv7` | every UUIDv7 array | SURVIVED |\n155|| `manifest.go:525` `checkContractAssertions` | contract encodings | SURVIVED |\n156|| `query.go:825` `checkTagsParameter` | `set_tags` tags | SURVIVED |\n157|| `query.go:927` `checkExecutePlanParameters` | confirmations | SURVIVED |\n158|| `query.go:1042` `checkUUIDv7DigestSubset` | `lineage_anchors` | SURVIVED |\n159|| `scan.go:438` `Journal.Import` | journal keys | SURVIVED |\n160|\n161|The census states this class as covered — shape 10, *\"ordering gates, not\n162|domain bounds, pinned by the sortedness refusal tests\"*. The sortedness refusal\n163|tests feed unsorted vectors (`[\"b\",\"a\"]`); none feeds a duplicate. This is\n164|leaf 1's \"class closed at one helper leaves the wrappers open\" recurring\n165|exactly, one abstraction level up.\n166|\n167|---\n168|\n169|## C4 (blocking) — `EncodeRequest`'s deadline ceiling has no driver, and its driver's comment says it does.\n170|\n171|`protocol.go:352` is a gate on the production host-side frame builder.\n172|Widening it survives under two spellings (`> MaxDeadlineMS+1`, `> 4000000`);\n173|the floor control (`< MinDeadlineMS-1`) dies, so the harness is live.\n174|\n175|The census names this a shape-7 stated bound \"pinned behaviourally by its named\n176|driver\". The driver, `TestUint53BoundEdges/request_deadline_ms`, is:\n177|\n178|```go\n179|if _, err := DecodeRequestFrame(...); err != nil {\n180|        return err          // <- returns here for 0 and for 3600001\n181|}\n182|_, err := EncodeRequest(...)\n183|return err\n184|```\n185|\n186|Both out-of-range literals are refused by the decode arm and return before\n187|`EncodeRequest` is ever called, so the builder is only ever driven with the two\n188|admitting values. The row's own comment claims the opposite: *\"a refusal from\n189|either entry fails the row.\"* A reported fact that measurement contradicts is a\n190|finding on its own.\n191|\n192|---\n193|\n194|## Verified good — do not re-litigate\n195|\n196|- Bound census: package-specific shape space, fails closed on unregistered\n197|  sites, orphan rows, helper aliases, empty scan; 11 canaries; three synthetic\n198|  derivation proofs. 68/94 on the rev1 denominator, 0 resurrections, every\n199|  survivor a verified equivalence.\n200|- `checkURI` wrapper closed in both directions — leaf 1's `requireStringBounds`\n201|  shape does not recur.\n202|- B3's own vector fixed and pinned by construction; the three rename→delete\n203|  conversions fixed and pinned by message.\n204|- 17/17 operation admissions derived from the production registry, failing\n205|  closed on a missing builder; `root`/`pwned`/`secret` all die.\n206|- 115 of 144 refusal arms die under deletion; the refusal-arm census itself,\n207|  the traceability re-pin, `Journal.Import`'s build-then-assign, and the README\n208|  claims were verified in rev1 and are unchanged.\n209|- Suite, vet, gofmt, and the 83.3% coverage figure all reproduce.\n210|\n211|## Scope note\n212|\n213|C1–C4 are evidence findings, not behaviour bugs: every gate named above refuses\n214|correctly in the shipped code. What is missing is the test that would fail if it\n215|stopped. Given two consecutive same-class rounds on C1 and C2, the next revision\n216|should add a derived gate for each class — arm-to-vector reachability, and an\n217|obligation roster for the operation validators — rather than more rows.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c585","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075af-a7c5-7382-ae46-5efb02855e33"},"sequence":285,"recorded_at":1780531400000565,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589"},"call_id":"call_01a075b0b3387a91816e8ebab4f73031","text":"Read text file `/tmp/ljkj8r/TASK-260830-ljkj8r_round2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework — review response (B1/B2/B3)\n2|\n3|Production code is unchanged from the reviewed candidate: all rework is\n4|tests plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes. Working tree holds the\n5|rework uncommitted per the brief.\n6|\n7|## B1 — bound instrument ported (blocking, now closed)\n8|\n9|- `internal/dirnode/bound_census_test.go`: production-derived bound census,\n10|  101 sites (9 helpers + len/length-var guards), 72 driven + 29 exempt\n11|  (mechanism/plumbing with rationale). Census fails closed on unregistered\n12|  sites, orphaned rows, helper aliases, and unscanned files.\n13|- `internal/dirnode/bounds_edge_test.go`: edge drivers for every driven row\n14|  (min-1/min/max/max+1 through the production entry).\n15|- Battery: 185 applied / 142 killed / 43 equivalent-with-bound / 0 survivors,\n16|  zero not-applied, zero compile failures. Denominator derived from\n17|  production (scanner output), not listed.\n18|- Census-only kills scored separately: 2 live census mutants redden only\n19|  `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused` (unregistered site; helper alias), plus the\n20|  three synthetic gate proofs. Behavioural kills (142) all fail a driver\n21|  that exercises the production entry.\n22|\n23|## B2 — seventeen-operation obligation set derived and driven (blocking, now closed)\n24|\n25|- `internal/dirnode/query_operations_test.go`: `TestDecodeQueryAllOperationsAdmit`\n26|  drives 17/17 registry members (was 5/17 reaching DecodeQuery) with kind\n27|  checks; `TestDecodeQueryOperationValidatorsRefuse` drives 40+\n28|  validator-specific defects; projection/sort/pagination/lineage/count\n29|  rules pinned alongside.\n30|- Zero-coverage functions before: validQueryField, checkLineageParameters,\n31|  checkHostsParameters, checkEnvironmentsParameters, checkJobsParameters,\n32|  checkPlansParameters, checkDistinctParameters, checkTagsParameter,\n33|  checkPinParameter, checkEnrichParameters (10 at 0.0%). After: none at 0.0%.\n34|- Review narrowing probes are battery rows V01 (environments/\"root\"),\n35|  V02 (jobs/\"pwned\"), V03 (distinct/\"secret\"): all killed.\n36|\n37|## B3 — arm-slide vectors fixed (blocking, now closed)\n38|\n39|- `unknown_field` rebuilt without the duplicate `fields` member; new\n40|  `TestUnknownFieldVectorReachesTheFieldRegistry` proves the operation\n41|  object passes the strict decoder (single `fields`) before DecodeQuery\n42|  refuses, so the field registry is reached, not the duplicate gate.\n43|- Audit found the same rename-instead-of-delete slide in three more\n44|  vectors (query \"missing caller\", manifest \"missing member\", probe\n45|  response \"missing member\"): each renamed member fired the unknown arm\n46|  while witnessing the missing arm. All three now delete the member, and\n47|  `TestMissingVectorsDriveTheMissingArm` asserts the missing-member message.\n48|- Scan/probe-request missing vectors already delete; unknown vectors add\n49|  exactly one member. Protocol `relabeled major pair` placeholder is\n50|  overridden with a genuine relabeled frame (verified, no change needed).\n51|\n52|## AC coverage — 9 of 9 rows driven through production entries\n53|\n54|| AC row | production call site | named test |\n55||---|---|---|\n56|| major bootstrap | DecideBootstrapStep/NextLowerMajor/ProcessGuard.Claim | TestBootstrapSelectsV2Directly, TestBootstrapFallsBackV2ToV1, TestNextLowerMajorBounds, TestProcessGuardRefusesReuse |\n57|| manifest framing | DecodeManifest/CheckManifestBindings/ManifestDigest | TestDecodeManifestClosedMemberRules, TestCheckManifestBindings, TestStringBoundEdges, TestDigestArrayBoundEdges, TestManifestLimitsBoundEdges, TestContractAssertionBoundEdges |\n58|| probe framing | CheckProbeRequest/CheckProbeResponse/CheckNodeBuildEqualsManifest | TestProbeRequestMajorVocabularies, TestProbeResponseFindingBound, TestProbeEnvironmentsBoundEdges, TestNodeBuildEqualityRefusesDrift |\n59|| scan framing | CheckScanRequest/CheckScanResponse | TestCheckScanRequestRefusals, TestCheckScanResponseRefusals, TestStringBoundEdges, TestDigestArrayBoundEdges, TestUint53BoundEdges |\n60|| query framing (17 ops) | DecodeQuery/CheckCursorReuse | TestDecodeQueryAllOperationsAdmit (17/17), TestDecodeQueryOperationValidatorsRefuse, TestDecodeQueryProjectionFields, TestCheckCursorReuse |\n61|| host checks | ProcessGuard, CheckManifestBindings, CheckCursorReuse | TestProcessGuardRefusesReuse, TestCheckManifestBindings, TestCheckCursorReuse |\n62|| structured errors | failX constructors via every entry | census TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed + arm witnesses |\n63|| crash/idempotency | Journal.CheckAndRecord/Export/Import | TestJournalSurvivesRestart, TestJournalImportRefusesUnsortedRecords, TestJournalBoundEdges |\n64|| no unsupported capability | Operations/FramedOperations/Capabilities/AvailableCapabilities | TestOperationRegistryDerivedFromSpec, TestFramedSubsetIsExact, TestAvailableCapabilitiesNeverUpgrades |\n65|\n66|## Evidence\n67|\n68|- `go test ./...`: 18 packages ok, 0 fail (exit 0).\n69|- `go test ./internal/dirnode/ -cover`: 83.3% statements (was 74.9%), zero functions at 0.0%.\n70|- `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`, `go build ./...`: exit 0.\n71|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck`: ok.\n72|- `gofmt -l internal/`: clean.\n73|\n74|# TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework — review response (B1/B2