{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075af-a7c5-7382-ae46-5efb02855e33"},"sequence":319,"recorded_at":1780531400000633,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"19faf56a-001a-4a1e-b080-b0c7556b3429"},"task_id":"19faf56a-001a-4a1e-b080-b0c7556b3429","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"19faf56a-001a-4a1e-b080-b0c7556b3429","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/ljkj8r/mutant-log-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-ljkj8r — reviewer mutant log rev2 (RUN-260906-8a5258)\n2|\n3|Harness: copy-aside / one-step edit / `go test ./internal/dirnode/ -count=1` /\n4|copy-back, byte-restore after every row. Production code is **byte-identical**\n5|to rev1 (`git diff 4d8a599 bd3cb8c` touches only test files, `LOGBOOK.md`), so\n6|every rev1 mutant coordinate still applies without re-anchoring: 0 NOT_APPLIED\n7|across all five batteries.\n8|\n9|Working tree verified equal to candidate tree\n10|`bd3cb8c05f421365e1e20f9e18ad53cb13d33d18` after the last row.\n11|\n12|Baseline: `go test ./... -count=1` 18 packages ok; `go vet ./...` exit 0;\n13|`gofmt -l internal/` clean; `go test ./internal/dirnode -cover` 83.3%.\n14|\n15|| battery | denominator derived from | applied | killed | survived | not applied | compile fail |\n16||---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n17|| 1. rev1 bound battery, re-run verbatim | production helper call sites | 94 | **68** | 26 | 0 | 0 |\n18|| 2. sites rev1 never touched (len guards, wrapper internals, shape-7/8/10 stated bounds) | production comparison sites | 54 | 42 | 12 | 0 | 0 |\n19|| 3. targeted follow-ups | — | 9 | 3 | 6 | 0 | 0 |\n20|| 4. refusal-arm reachability (every `if` whose body builds a `failX`) | production AST | 144 | 115 | 29 | 0 | 0 |\n21|| 5. query operation obligations (every `return false` in query.go) | production AST | 89 | 58 | 31 | 0 | 0 |\n22|\n23|Census-only kills: **0**. Every kill I recorded names at least one behavioural\n24|driver; the four rows that redden `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused` (B12, B13, B21,\n25|B24) each also redden a behavioural test in the same run.\n26|\n27|## Battery 1 — rev1 battery re-run (68/94, was 19/94)\n28|\n29|Zero resurrections: all 19 rev1 kills are still killed. The 26 survivors map\n30|1:1 onto declared `equiv-ok` rows in `TASK-260830-ljkj8r_round2.md`, and each\n31|masking gate was verified in production source rather than accepted from the\n32|rationale:\n33|\n34|| survivor class | rows | masking gate verified |\n35||---|---:|---|\n36|| `requested_environment_ids` / `environment_ids` element floor+ceiling | 4 | `environmentIDPattern` `^[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}$` — 0 and 65 both unmatchable |\n37|| `provider_ids` element floor+ceiling | 2 | `providerIDPattern` `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$` |\n38|| closed-vocabulary element floor/ceiling + Nth-member count (`requested_capabilities`, `scopes`, `authentication_status`, `job states`, `enrich kinds`) | 13 | `validCapability` over the 8-name `capabilityOrder`; the 5/4/7/3-member tables; Nth valid member unbuildable under sorted-unique |\n39|| `supported_versions` element floor 5→4 | 1 | `checkSemver` — shortest SemVer is 5 characters |\n40|| projection `fields` element floor/ceiling + count | 3 | 27-member `queryFields` registry |\n41|| batch `operations` ceiling 64→65 and `index` ceiling 63→64 | 2 | joint gate: the pair coincide at 65; both tightenings die (B28, B30) |\n42|| `native_observation_ids` count 65536→65537 | 1 | stated bound (65537-element body not built) |\n43|\n44|No false equivalence found.\n45|\n46|## Battery 2/3 — sites rev1 never touched\n47|\n48|Killed (42): `checkURI` ceiling both directions, extension key 253 both\n49|directions and floor tightening, contract assertion 15/64 all four directions,\n50|`checkNestedObjects` caller literals both directions, findings 4096 both\n51|directions, `MaxFrameBytes`, `MaxDeadlineMS`, `MinDeadlineMS`, both frame\n52|`>` → `>=` tightenings, batch floor/ceiling tightening, `index` tightening,\n53|tags 256 both directions, confirmations 64 both directions, `skip` 1000000\n54|both directions, `take` 1/1000 all three, sort 8 both directions, cursor\n55|1/1024 all three, journal version gate both spellings, all three bootstrap\n56|exit-status gates, `checkSortedUniqueStrings` uniqueness.\n57|\n58|Survivors requiring a finding are listed in the verdict. The remainder are\n59|verified-equivalent: `checkURI` floor `<1`→`<2` (2-character `a:` admits under\n60|both; `<1`→`<4` dies, C09), extension key floor `<3`→`<2` (reverse-DNS minimum\n61|is `a.b`), and the joint batch/index pair above.\n62|\n63|## Battery 4 — refusal-arm reachability, 144 arms, 29 survive\n64|\n65|`if <cond> { … failX … }` → `if false && (<cond>) { … }`, i.e. the arm is\n66|removed while every other arm stays. A survivor means no committed test would\n67|notice the arm's removal.\n68|\n69|| survivor group | arms | site |\n70||---|---:|---|\n71|| envelope `unknownMember` | 3 | `manifest.go:268`, `probe.go:338`, `query.go:415` |\n72|| envelope `missingMember` | 5 | `probe.go:141`, `protocol.go:428`, `protocol.go:559`, `scan.go:78`, `scan.go:193` |\n73|| `checkExtensions` | 2 | `probe.go:392` (probe response), `query.go:467` (query envelope) |\n74|| empty-frame guard | 3 | `bootstrap.go:144`, `protocol.go:399`, `protocol.go:530` |\n75|| strict-decode `fault != nil` masked by a downstream member arm | 8 | `manifest.go:261`, `probe.go:127`, `probe.go:331`, `protocol.go:545`, `query.go:408`, `scan.go:64`, `scan.go:179`, `scan.go:395` |\n76|| envelope member-read `!ok` / `!present` masked downstream | 6 | `manifest.go:329`, `manifest.go:337`, `protocol.go:443`, `protocol.go:474`, `protocol.go:639`, `protocol.go:684` |\n77|| marshal/parse `err != nil` | 2 | `protocol.go:377`, `scan.go:365` |\n78|\n79|## Battery 5 — query operation obligations, 89 sites, 31 survive\n80|\n81|`return false` → `return true`, one site per row: the obligation is removed and\n82|every sibling stays.\n83|\n84|| validator | obligations | driven | undriven |\n85||---|---:|---:|---:|\n86|| `checkPlanContinueParameters` | 9 | 3 | 6 |\n87|| `checkQuerySort` | 8 | 3 | 5 |\n88|| `checkFilters` | 16 | 13 | 3 |\n89|| `checkQueryParameters` | 5 | 2 | 3 |\n90|| `checkExecutePlanParameters` | 5 | 2 | 3 |\n91|| `checkSubject` | 4 | 1 | 3 |\n92|| `checkUUIDv7DigestSubset` | 5 | 3 | 2 |\n93|| `checkQueryFlags` | 3 | 1 | 2 |\n94|| `checkTagsParameter` | 3 | 2 | 1 |\n95|| `checkLineageParameters` | 2 | 1 | 1 |\n96|| `checkDistinctParameters` | 2 | 1 | 1 |\n97|| `isAnnotationMutation` | 1 | 0 | 1 |\n98|| 11 validators at full coverage (`checkEnvironmentsParameters`, `checkJobsParameters`, `checkQueryProjection`, `checkEnrichParameters`, `checkPlansParameters`, `checkEnumSubset`, `checkQueryPagination`, `isListOperation`, `validQueryField`, `validQueryPreset`, `checkHostsParameters`) | 26 | 26 | 0 |\n99|| **total** | **89** | **58** | **31** |\n100|\n101|## Direct production probes (unmutated, through the production entry)\n102|\n103|| probe | observed refusal |\n104||---|---|\n105|| manifest `unknown member` vector (`manifest_test.go:62`) | `node manifest trailing data after the object` — the strict-decode arm, not `unknownMember` |\n106|| query `unknown member` vector (`query_test.go:75`) | `directory query operation is not a closed QueryOperation` — the operation arm; the needle matched `operations[0].parameters` |\n107|| probe-response `unknown member` vector (`probe_test.go:142`) | `probe response node build is not the closed DirectoryNodeBuild` — the node-build arm; the needle matched `node_build` |\n108|| probe request / scan request / scan response / request-frame `missing member` vectors | all four report `misses a required member` — the vectors are built correctly; the assertions do not discriminate the arm |\n109|| probe response `extensions:{\"NOTDNS\":{}}` | `probe response extensions are not reverse-DNS keyed` — the gate works, nothing drives it |\n110|| `EncodeRequest(MajorV2, manifest, id, 3600001, {})` | refused today; `TestUint53BoundEdges` never calls it with that value |"}}}
