{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c78b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075af-a7c5-7382-ae46-5efb02855e33"},"sequence":544,"recorded_at":1780531400001083,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"99d33263-dfac-4e6d-9d13-f0eaceb3b227"},"task_id":"99d33263-dfac-4e6d-9d13-f0eaceb3b227","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"99d33263-dfac-4e6d-9d13-f0eaceb3b227","chunk":"Read text file `internal/dirnode/census_test.go`.\n1|package dirnode\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"go/ast\"\n5|\t\"go/parser\"\n6|\t\"go/token\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\t\"path/filepath\"\n9|\t\"sort\"\n10|\t\"strconv\"\n11|\t\"strings\"\n12|\t\"testing\"\n13|)\n14|\n15|// This file is the derived refusal-arm inventory. It exists\n16|// because a new refusal through an existing site — a widened\n17|// member set, a new detail literal, a dropped check that slides\n18|// to a lower arm — leaves the whole suite green unless the arm\n19|// set is derived from production source by parsing it, never by\n20|// listing it.\n21|//\n22|// Derivation (deriveRefusalArms): every call to one of the eight\n23|// refusal constructors with a string-literal first argument\n24|// yields ctor|<constructor>|<detail>; a call whose first argument\n25|// is a binary expression yields\n26|// ctor|<constructor>|expr|<function>|<rendered>, where the render\n27|// keeps literal text, identifier names, and selector paths, so a\n28|// context-prefixed envelope arm and a fault-detail conduit never\n29|// merge with each other or with a literal arm; every\n30|// &frameFault{...} literal yields frame|<detail>. A constructor\n31|// call with any other first-argument shape is a derivation\n32|// violation, not a silent pass. Constructor references outside\n33|// direct-call position fail the derivation outright: an aliased\n34|// constructor hides every arm it builds. All alias spellings are\n35|// caught — `alias := failX`, `var alias = failX` at package\n36|// level, `var alias = failX` inside a function body, arguments,\n37|// returns, struct fields, assignments — because the gate exempts\n38|// only the definition's own Name in its ValueSpec, never a\n39|// constructor identifier appearing anywhere else. The\n40|// constructors of this package are themselves declared as\n41|// `var failX = func...`, so their definition Names stay exempt\n42|// while any other reference fails. A refusal call inside any\n43|// function literal that is not a registered constructor body\n44|// fails: an arm that fires only when a closure runs is not a\n45|// call-site arm.\n46|//\n47|// The constructor denominator is itself derived, not listed on\n48|// trust: TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction requires the\n49|// registered set to equal the eight named constructors, every\n50|// axerror.New site in production to sit inside one registered\n51|// body, and no func-value indirection of axerror.New anywhere.\n52|// A ninth constructor, an inline axerror.New refusal, or a\n53|// `var newFault = axerror.New` indirection carries an additive\n54|// arm the derivation never observes, and fails there instead of\n55|// passing silently.\n56|//\n57|// Both directions are checked:\n58|// TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed (every derived arm\n59|// carries a witness) and TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived (every\n60|// witness names a derived arm, so a truncated derivation reddens\n61|// on the orphaned witnesses instead of passing vacuously).\n62|// TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry is intentionally\n63|// a resolve-and-run check rather than prose: every witness names\n64|// test functions that exist in this package's test files, and\n65|// those tests drive the production entries with negative vectors\n66|// asserting code plus distinguishing detail. Empty, single-file,\n67|// or unparseable derivations fail closed: a domain that silently\n68|// derives nothing is not a measurement.\n69|//\n70|// Shape space. An error construction in this package can only be\n71|// carried by these AST shapes; the census derives or refuses each\n72|// one:\n73|//\n74|//  1. A direct `failX(\"literal\", ...)` call — DERIVED as an arm\n75|//     keyed by the literal detail.\n76|//  2. A direct `failX(<binary>, ...)` call — DERIVED as an arm\n77|//     keyed by function and rendered expression. The two\n78|//     sub-shapes in production are the fault-detail conduit\n79|//     (`\"prefix \"+fault.detail`, eleven sites) and the\n80|//     envelope-branch prefix (`context+\" suffix\"`, eleven\n81|//     sites in checkResponseIdentity); both render distinctly,\n82|//     so neither merges.\n83|//  3. A direct `failX(<other>, ...)` call — REFUSED as a\n84|//     derivation violation (zero such sites exist; the first\n85|//     one fails the census instead of passing silently).\n86|//  4. A package-level `var failY = func...` literal whose body\n87|//     calls axerror.New — DERIVED as a constructor: the\n88|//     produced set must equal refusalConstructors exactly, so\n89|//     a ninth constructor fails as unregistered.\n90|//  5. An axerror.New call outside every registered literal —\n91|//     REFUSED as a construction site outside the registered\n92|//     bodies.\n93|//  6. An axerror.New selector in non-call position (alias var,\n94|//     returned constructor, argument, struct field) — REFUSED\n95|//     as a func-value indirection (the import census pins the\n96|//     `axerror` binding it matches on).\n97|//  7. A failX identifier in non-call, non-definition position\n98|//     (alias var/:=, assignment, argument, return, struct\n99|//     field) — REFUSED as a constructor alias that would bury\n100|//     every arm built through it.\n101|//  8. A failX call inside a non-constructor function literal —\n102|//     REFUSED as a closure-hidden arm.\n103|//  9. An import of the error package path under any other name\n104|//     — REFUSED by the import census\n105|//     (TestAxerrorImportsAreUnaliased pins the `axerror`\n106|//     binding every identifier match above relies on).\n107|//  10. A &frameFault{...} literal — DERIVED as a frame arm by\n108|//     its literal detail.\n109|//\n110|// 10 of 10 shapes derived-or-refused. The residue, stated here\n111|// rather than left silent: a frameFault built through a type\n112|// alias (`type ff = frameFault`) would hide from shape 10 — no\n113|// such alias exists in production (the derivation fails on any\n114|// CompositeLit it cannot classify, but an alias retypes the\n115|// node it matches, so this bound is textual: grep finds no\n116|// `frameFault` alias); a construction via assembly, linkname,\n117|// or reflect would hide from shapes 5-6 — the package uses none\n118|// of those mechanisms; files outside the package directory and\n119|// _test.go files, which the census never scans, must not carry\n120|// production refusals — TestCensusScansEveryProductionFile\n121|// requires the scanned set to equal the production file list\n122|// the package build sees; a second argument that smuggles the\n123|// distinguishing fact while the first stays constant would make\n124|// two arms share one key — the constructors' second parameters\n125|// are wire facts asserted selectively by the entry tests, never\n126|// the arm identity, and the witness table records the\n127|// code-plus-detail pair per arm.\n128|//\n129|// Census-only kills score separately from behavioural ones:\n130|// every arm the derivation observes reddens the census by\n131|// construction when its site is edited, and that reddening\n132|// proves the census runs, not that the gate refuses. Behavioural\n133|// proof stays with each row's named witness, which the inventory\n134|// resolves textually and runs as part of the suite.\n135|\n136|// refusalConstructors is the exact registered constructor set.\n137|// Each must be a package-level `var failX = func...` whose body\n138|// calls axerror.New; the derivation verifies both halves.\n139|var refusalConstructors = []string{\n140|\t\"failInvalid\",\n141|\t\"failViolation\",\n142|\t\"failUnknownOperation\",\n143|\t\"failDowngrade\",\n144|\t\"failIntegrity\",\n145|\t\"failIdempotency\",\n146|\t\"failQuery\",\n147|\t\"failTransport\",\n148|}\n149|\n150|// parseGoFile parses one Go source file for the censuses.\n151|func parseGoFile(path string, source []byte) (*ast.File, error) {\n152|\treturn parser.ParseFile(token.NewFileSet(), path, source, 0)\n153|}\n154|\n155|// productionFiles returns the production file paths of this\n156|// package directory: every non-test Go file. Test files are\n157|// never scanned: a refusal built in a test helper is not a\n158|// production arm.\n159|func productionFiles(t *testing.T) []string {\n160|\tt.Helper()\n161|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n162|\tif err != nil {\n163|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"census: %v\", err)\n164|\t}\n165|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n166|\tif err != nil {\n167|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"census: %v\", err)\n168|\t}\n169|\tvar files []string\n170|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n171|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n172|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n173|\t\t\tcontinue\n174|\t\t}\n175|\t\tfiles = append(files, filepath.Join(directory, name))\n176|\t}\n177|\tsort.Strings(files)\n178|\tif len(files) == 0 {\n179|\t\tt.Fatal(\"census scanned zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n180|\t}\n181|\treturn files\n182|}\n183|\n184|// armDerivation is the derived inventory plus every shape\n185|// violation found along the way.\n186|type armDerivation struct {\n187|\tarms       map[string]bool\n188|\tctors      map[string]bool\n189|\tviolations []string\n190|}\n191|\n192|// deriveRefusalArms parses every production file and derives the\n193|// constructor set, the arm set, and the violation list.\n194|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) armDerivation {\n195|\tt.Helper()\n196|\tderived := armDerivation{arms: map[string]bool{}, ctors: map[string]bool{}}\n197|\tfor _, path := range productionFiles(t) {\n198|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n199|\t\tif err != nil {\n200|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"census: %v\", err)\n(more lines below)"}}}
