{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e2a5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075af-a7c5-7382-ae46-5efb02855e33"},"sequence":4013,"recorded_at":1780531400008021,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f1bef9f3-46dc-4d65-b0f2-5e22216e1589"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Round 3 rework is handed off to review (`to-review`, checklist 18/18).\n\nWhat was done, per finding:\n\n- **C1**: fixed the 3 misdirected unknown-member vectors to append at the true top level; replaced the false \"one member per vector\" claim with `arm_reachability_test.go` — 146 rows pairing each production-derived arm key with a firing vector, matched on the full derived refusal rendering (code + wrapper from constructor bodies, detail/prefix from arm keys), failing closed on undetermined reaches, orphaned rows, and missing vectors. Arm battery: **142/144 killed**, 2 survivors are the defensive marshal arms.\n- **C2**: `obligation_census_test.go` derives all 112 false-returns in `query.go` (the 89 plus the same-shaped caller/operation tuple sites) with one narrow `DecodeQuery` vector each. Battery: **111/112 behaviorally killed**; sole survivor is the unreachable registry-divergence site, bounded by a table-agreement tripwire. Killer-set mapping shows 1:1 narrowness plus only the documented framing-gate ANDs and layered delegate pairs.\n- **C3**: `TestSortedUniqueDuplicatesRefuse` feeds duplicates at all 8 scans with dedup controls; **8/8 narrowing kills**, each 1:1. Shape-10 claim corrected.\n- **C4**: deadline row drives decode and encode entries independently with a corrected comment, plus a direct encode-ceiling refusal; **2/2 widenings killed**.\n\nVerification I ran myself: full arm (144), obligation (112), uniqueness (8), and deadline (2) batteries; repo-wide suite green across 18 packages, vet/gofmt clean, dirnode coverage 87.6%. Production code is byte-identical to the round-2 baseline (hashes in the outcome doc); no resurrections. Evidence attached: `TASK-260830-ljkj8r_round3.md` + arms/obligations killer tables.","reason":null}}
